{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix bridge-test modules contain repeated, historical, decorative, contradictory, or obvious prose. Their blobs are unchanged from the audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only the listed blocks. Preserve non-docstring AST/runtime strings, assertions, external citations, and exact directives.\n\n## Scope\n- `test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:1-22,34-49,181-196,287-292,331-352,389-441,465-470,520,525-531,561-566,591,594-600,639,642-650,683-689,719-724,744-755` — Preserve exact ACLI payload/argv, REST routing, sanitizer boundaries, and citations to Atlassian threads 3237097/989632 and `tenable/integration-jira-cloud#322`; remove decorative banners and code restatements.\n- `test_bridge_alert_display.py:1-32,44-50,59-61,114-116,157-159,218-220,226,244-246,259,294,304-306,318,353` — Preserve alert resolution and show/list projection contracts; correct the contradictory “key absent” wording to match required-key assertions; remove banners/obvious narration.\n- `test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py:1-9,138-185,191-194,211-213,416-418` — Preserve that window absence is informational and only persisted confirmed-404 state establishes dangling drift.\n- `test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev_heldout.py:169-180,254-261` — Preserve payload-byte versus logical ref-state comparison.\n- `test_bridge_fsck_repair.py:1-13` — Preserve exact audited-set pruning and all four pre-write guards.\n- `test_jira_capability_probe.py:18-20,26-28,64-68,77-79,83,97,126-127,158-159,168-170,284-287,300-311` — Preserve both import seams (`sys.modules` and package attribute), capability setup, and logical retry schedule; remove banners and repeated setup narration.\n\nConsumers are pytest, the focused bridge suite, and `check_comment_hygiene.py`; no target-specific runtime docstring reader exists. Preserve the four probe `type: ignore` directives byte-for-byte and attached to their statements.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only reviewed comments/true docstrings or blank lines change; normalized non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and exact statement-attached directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] An independent reviewer posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block, pinned before and immutable final-commit after citations, preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, and `semantic-preservation` plus `bloat-removal` verdicts.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and removes repetition/history/ornament rather than relocating it; every TSV row is PASS.\n- [ ] Recorded focused hermetic checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n- [ ] Missing/FAIL rows or unmatched diff hunks block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, focused tests, diff check, and `make verify`. The independent TSV judges prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788613344702831001,"uuid":"acef9f5f-cb95-4706-b537-c584a5a2011e"}